From 6cb344e208949bf0ce501402fffa47e07b5cf700 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Claude <noreply@anthropic.com>
Date: Fri, 25 Sep 2026 23:15:38 +0000
Subject: [PATCH 4/4] Performance B: gentler culling, skip silent effect
 chains, one pass less

- Culling (ported from upstream #4819 and its predecessors onto 1.2.1's
  cullVoice()): soft culls only while the overload persists and isn't
  falling; hard culls from 32 samples over the limit (was 20) with half as
  many voices (over >> 4), one released softly, half of the rest faded out
  within a few ms and half stopped at once (was: all stopped at once);
  20 samples of extra allowance per voice started in the measured render
  (up to 4).
- Kits and audio tracks skip their effect chain while nothing comes in and
  the chain has given out exact silence for 4096 samples, as long as it
  holds nothing that could still sound or move on (mod FX, delay, stutter,
  sample rate reduction, saturation, compressor, recording). Sidechain,
  volume ramp state, reverb activity and parameter ticking carry on.
- Without compressor and recording, the post-FX volume stage of sounds,
  kits and audio tracks adds straight into the output instead of writing
  the buffer back and adding it in a second pass.
- The kit/audio-track effects buffer is raw storage, so it isn't zeroed a
  second time by StereoSample's initialisers.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
Claude-Session: https://claude.ai/code/session_01Eb214cM1zi1k5Gpcn9RLKh
